dius are all **0**. A monolithic schema may also be easier for tooling and validation; size alone does not justify splitting it.\n\n- `src/esbuild/svelte.ts`: **1 direct / 7 transitive importers** and functions of 116, 106, and 91 lines, largely overlapping. It has complete reported test coverage and considerably less connectivity than the first four targets.\n\n- `src/rollup/ts-resolve.ts`: **1 direct / 1 transitive importer**; its 88- and 77-line findings overlap and have low blast radius.\n\n- `src/esbuild/swc.ts`, `src/plugins/swc-target.ts`, and `src/plugins/terser.ts`: their functions are only **65, 62, and 62 lines**—barely over the threshold. Do not create abstraction churn merely to cross a line-count boundary.\n\nThe intended sequence is therefore: dismantle the high-fan-out orchestrators first, then narrow the high-fan-in shared modules behind stable façades. Re-scan after each file-level extraction to confirm that fan-out moves into cohesive modules rather than merely being redistributed.",
